# .git-blame-ignore-revs — commits that should be skipped by `git blame`.
#
# Add commits that are pure churn (formatting sweeps, whitespace fixes,
# mechanical renames) here so blame points at the meaningful change, not
# the sweep. Optional: enable in your local config with
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# (This file is the repo-side record; the config command above is a
# per-developer convenience and is intentionally NOT committed.)